{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Group G of the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] began on 13 June and completed on 23 June 2006. [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]] won the group and advanced to the [[2006 FIFA World Cup#Round of 16|round of 16]], along with [[France national football team|France]], who went on to reach the final. [[South Korea national football team|South Korea]] and [[Togo national football team|Togo]] failed to advance.<ref>{{cite web |last=Saaid |first=Hamdan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2006full.html |title=World Cup 2006 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=7 February 2007 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> Switzerland were the only team not to concede a goal during the group stage of the tournament and would become the first team to be knocked out of a [[FIFA World Cup|World Cup]] without conceding, losing on penalties after a 0–0 draw with [[Ukraine national football team|Ukraine]] in the round of 16.

